 "content_notes": "Tone: absurd and ironic about failed ramps. No weapon is drawn or pointed and no violence is shown; the agents hold only flashlights. The smugglers and runners were never identified: they appear only as anonymous dark silhouettes (no face, ethnicity or costume). The agents and the young man in the lesson are generic figures, never named; no badge, flag, patch or insignia of any real agency; no logo. The vehicles are generic unbadged SUVs and a plain truck; 'Jeep' is said and never drawn as a logo or grille. Marijuana is shown only as plain taped bundles. The 2012 Jeep was empty when found; the narration does not say it carried drugs. Every card is our own typed graphic. The only quotation is the Border Patrol's statement as reported by NPR, RIA Novosti and CNN. Status verified 2026-10-17.",
