 "claims": [
  {
   "id": "K_hook",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "In late October 2012 smugglers drove a Jeep Cherokee up a homemade ramp onto the roughly 14-foot border fence and it got stuck (high-centered) on top. Narration: 'Smugglers drove their Jeep up the border fence.' / 'It got stuck. On top. 14 feet up.'",
   "sources": [
    "npr",
    "fox13",
    "cbs",
    "pnt",
    "foxnews",
    "ria",
    "eidaho"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_place",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "Yuma Sector: the Imperial Sand Dunes, California, about five miles west of the Colorado River and the Arizona line (AP caption and CNN: 'near Yuma, Ariz.'); spotted early on Tuesday 30 October 2012. Label 'YUMA SECTOR · OCT 2012'.",
   "sources": [
    "cbs",
    "eidaho",
    "ria",
    "fox13",
    "leadstories"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_fled",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "Two men on the Mexican side who were trying to free the Jeep fled into Mexico when agents approached; no arrests. Narration: 'But agents came. Both men fled into Mexico.'",
   "sources": [
    "cbs",
    "fox13",
    "ria",
    "eidaho"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_verdict",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "FUN FACT CARD (wording as reported in two independent outlets): Border Patrol said the smugglers 'fell prey to their own devices' with 'a make-shift ramp that was not quite up to the task.' Narration: 'Border Patrol's verdict? Not quite up to the task.'",
   "sources": [
    "npr",
    "ria",
    "fox13"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_seized12",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "Agents removed the Jeep from the fence and seized it and both ramps; the Jeep was empty. End label 'SEIZED: THE JEEP + BOTH RAMPS'.",
   "sources": [
    "cbs",
    "foxnews",
    "eidaho",
    "ria"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_truck",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "April 2011, Barry M. Goldwater Range east of Yuma, Arizona: agents found a folding ramp extending over the border fence from a large truck parked on the Mexican side (AP: a truck with ramps built onto it). Narration: 'But that was not their wildest ramp.' / 'In 2011, a truck brought a folding ramp.'",
   "sources": [
    "swj",
    "hsnw",
    "cbs",
    "insight"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_1000",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "STATISTIC (counter): a Jeep Cherokee had apparently just used the ramp to carry about 1,000 lb of marijuana across; over 1,000 lb was seized on the range (7 April 2011) and the two suspects fled back into Mexico, leaving the vehicle. Narration: 'A Jeep crossed with 1,000 pounds of weed.' Counter '1,000 LB'.",
   "sources": [
    "mcas",
    "swj",
    "hsnw"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_eleven",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "February 2019, Cabeza Prieta National Wildlife Refuge (Ajo station, Arizona): a heavily modified Jeep Cherokee carrying 11 people and suspected bundles of marijuana, spotted by a helicopter crew, tried a homemade ramp over the vehicle barrier and got stuck. Narration: 'In 2019, eleven people in one Jeep.' / 'Its homemade ramp failed. Stuck again.'",
   "sources": [
    "kxxv",
    "kgun",
    "ktar",
    "sentinel"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_eleven_fled",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "All 11 fled into Mexico on foot; Mexican officials searched and found neither the people nor the drugs; agents seized the Jeep.",
   "sources": [
    "kxxv",
    "ktar",
    "sentinel"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_punch",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "In all three cases the people got away (2012: two men; April 2011: two suspects; 2019: eleven people) and the Jeep was left behind and seized. Narration: 'Every driver escaped.' / 'The Jeeps never did.'",
   "sources": [
    "cbs",
    "fox13",
    "mcas",
    "swj",
    "kxxv",
    "ktar",
    "sentinel"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_lesson",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "LESSON CARD (practical, for the viewer): cartel recruiters on social media promise 'quick, easy money' to drive across or near the border, and smuggling is a felony (CBP / Border Patrol); CBP 'blind mule' advice: inspect any vehicle you drive before and after every trip and never carry items of unknown content for others; UK FCDO: you are responsible for anything you carry across a border, even if it belongs to someone else. Rows: 'EASY MONEY' DM = RED FLAG / CHECK ANY CAR YOU DRIVE / YOU OWN WHAT YOU CARRY.",
   "sources": [
    "cbp_teens",
    "scripps",
    "borderreport",
    "foxrgv",
    "inews",
    "fcdo"
   ]
  }
 ],
